  "articleBody": "Swapping an old tub for a modern walk-in shower is one of the best ways to upgrade comfort and accessibility. However, wet areas allow zero margin for error during construction.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid:\n- Ignoring concealed subfloor damage: Leaks often hide under old tub liners. Never place a new shower pan over soft, stained, or rotted plywood without repairing the subfloor and framing first.\n- Breaking the waterproofing continuity: Shower conversions require seamless, approved waterproofing membranes on walls and pan transitions. Skipping proper backing boards or membrane overlaps leads to hidden wall rot.\n- Moving drains without checking pipe slope: Shower drains require larger capacities than standard tub drains. Altering drain placement without maintaining proper pitch causes slow drainage and standing water.\n- Damaging shutoff valves during demolition: Ripping out tubs aggressively can bend or fracture copper lines behind the wall. Always disconnect fixtures carefully with proper trade tools.\n- Disposing of the tub prematurely: Make sure your replacement shower components, valve rough-ins, and wall panels match your exact rough framing opening before the old unit leaves the property.\n\nGetting proper trade permits and water testing protects your home against costly moisture issues. Call Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to handle your tub removal and custom shower installation.",
